      "hints": [
        "Equate $3x^2 - 4x + 4 = mx + m - 1 \\implies 3x^2 - (m + 4)x + (5 - m) = 0$.",
        "Set discriminant $\\Delta = (m + 4)^2 - 12(5 - m) > 0 \\implies m^2 + 20m - 44 > 0$.",
        "Factorise $(m + 22)(m - 2) > 0$ and state outside intervals."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Equate the curve and straight line equations:\n$$3x^2 - 4x + 4 = mx + m - 1 \\implies 3x^2 - (m + 4)x + (5 - m) = 0$$",
        "Set the discriminant $\\Delta > 0$ for two distinct points of intersection:\n$$\\Delta = [-(m + 4)]^2 - 4(3)(5 - m) > 0$$\n$$(m^2 + 8m + 16) - 12(5 - m) > 0 \\implies m^2 + 8m + 16 - 60 + 12m > 0$$\n$$m^2 + 20m - 44 > 0$$",
        "Factorise the quadratic inequality:\n$$(m + 22)(m - 2) > 0$$",
        "State the outside solution intervals:\n$$m < -22 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad m > 2$$"
      ],
